# Normalise text files in the repository and check Go sources out with LF endings.
#
# The index already stores LF (git's autocrlf=true handles that), but without this
# file every checkout writes CRLF into the working tree, which makes `gofmt -l`
# report ~25 untouched Go files as unformatted. Pinning eol=lf keeps the working
# tree identical to the index for Go code.
*.go text eol=lf

# Lockfiles and generated assets must never be rewritten.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary